Package: gamlssPosthoc
Type: Package
Title: Marginal, Distributional, and Graphical Post-Hoc Inference for GAMLSS Models
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(given = c("Walter", "Esfrain"), family = "Pereira",
    email = "walterufpb@yahoo.com.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191"))
Description: Provides a conservative post-hoc and visualization workflow for
    generalized additive models for location, scale and shape (GAMLSS). The
    package separates estimands, target populations, contrast scales, and
    uncertainty layers; routes supported operations to 'emmeans' or
    'marginaleffects'; reconstructs full predictive distributions for derived
    quantities and zero-adjusted models; and supplies an auditable 'ggplot2'
    data-first graphics layer for distributional parameters, marginal
    estimands, contrasts, predictive densities, quantile fans, trends,
    derivatives, optima, surfaces, fit diagnostics, and model comparisons.
    Methods follow the distributional-regression principles of Rigby and
    Stasinopoulos (2005) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9876.2005.00510.x> and the
    model-interpretation principles of Arel-Bundock, Greifer and Heiss (2024)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v111.i09>.
